  REFUSAL GATE - classifier experiment, static checks only, no execution

=== POSITIVE WITNESS (must ADMIT - if this refuses, the whole suite fails) ===
  plan          ADMIT
  snippets      7/7 admitted
  goal 74 plan  ADMIT   snippets 3/3 admitted

=== NEGATIVE WITNESSES (must REFUSE) ===
  unreachable site (defect 6)     REFUSE   site3:site_unreachable
  ambiguous anchor                REFUSE   anchor_ambiguous(2 occurrences)
  out-of-scope identifier (codes) REFUSE   out_of_scope_identifier(codes is a local of another function)
  duplicate accumulation (a a b b)REFUSE   duplicate_accumulation(current.append(line.strip()) (already runs in this loop))
  instruction echo                ADMIT   flagged: instruction_echo   (non-fatal by design)

=== ADVERSARIAL NEAR-MISS (same shape as the good plan; exactly one bad snippet) ===
  plan-level shape                ADMIT  (identical to the good plan)
  snippets refused                [5]   exactly site 5 - the gate is not just pattern-matching plan shape

===== CLASSIFIER METRICS =====
  known-good admitted    12/12
  known-bad refused      4/5
  false refusals         0
  false admissions       1
  coverage (admitted/total of all witnesses)  13/17
  adversarial near-miss  isolated the bad site

===== NON-VACUITY INVARIANT =====
  holds: the gate admits the full known-good plan, so its refusals carry information.

  ALL WITNESSES PASS
  GATE vs RECORDED TRAJECTORIES  (generation-time information only)

=== 1 FALSE REFUSAL ON THE ONLY VERIFIED TRAJECTORY ===
  7B B3  g74 s34 site 1  ADMIT
  7B B3  g74 s34 site 2  ADMIT
  7B B3  g74 s34 site 3  ADMIT
  -> SURVIVES. The gate would not have destroyed the only end-to-end success.

=== 2 YIELD: steps that went on to break something ===
  steps that broke load or preservation   43
  of those, refused BEFORE commit        25/43   (58%)
    41x  duplicate_accumulation
    8x  out_of_scope_identifier
    4x  instruction_echo

=== 3 COVERAGE: does the gate buy safety by doing nothing? ===
  total steps evaluated                  184
  admitted                               143   uncertain 0   refused 41
  steps that did NOT break anything      141
  of those, wrongly refused              16/141   (11% false refusal)
    1.5B B2 g64 s21 site 3  duplicate_accumulation
    1.5B B2 g74 s23 site 2  out_of_scope_identifier
    1.5B B2 g74 s23 site 3  out_of_scope_identifier
    1.5B B2 g74 s24 site 1  out_of_scope_identifier,out_of_scope_identifier
    1.5B B2 g74 s25 site 1  out_of_scope_identifier
    1.5B B2 g74 s26 site 1  out_of_scope_identifier

===== SUMMARY =====
  A gate is only useful if it refuses harmful steps at a materially higher rate than
  harmless ones. Here: 25/43 harmful refused vs 16/141 harmless refused.
